{"id": "EUVD-2026-103503", "enisaUuid": "6d97e3cb-4b21-35a7-b734-0c380cac1a43", "description": "librtmp (RTMPDump) through 2.6 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in AMFProp_Decode that reads an AMF0 strict-array element count before checking that four bytes remain. A malicious RTMP server or man in the middle can send an AMF0 body ending with a strict-array type byte and fewer than four trailing bytes to crash the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:37:50", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/librtmp-amf3-decode-and-strict-array-oob", "https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/rtmpdump.git/blob/138fdb258d9fc26f1843fd1b891180416c9dc575:/librtmp/amf.c", "https://rtmpdump.mplayerhq.hu/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/librtmp-rtmpdump-through-2.6-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-amfprop-decode"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m837-gfcx-6jp4", "CVE-2026-112061"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "345cb162-1731-3155-9214-dc95dc63be96", "product": {"name": "librtmp", "vendor": {"name": "RTMPDump"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "803a47d5-9487-329f-92cc-47d314f55b68", "vendor": {"name": "RTMPDump"}}], "isExploited": false}